# What each secret is and where it goes. Engine: repo-secrets (devbox
# docs/repo-secrets.md). One row per line:
#
#   target | source | mode | kind [| recipients]
#
#   file    target = plaintext path, source = its .age; materialized by decrypt
#   sshkey  like file, and decrypt regenerates target.pub
#   env     a KEY=VALUE secret kept off disk; target and mode are `-`
#   render  target = a generated env file, source = `a + b + …` (committed
#           config env files and/or `env` .age files); no recipients column
#
# The optional recipients column names secrets/recipients.<set>.txt, whose
# members read the row on top of the owners in secrets/recipients.txt.
#
# Example:
#   -             | secrets/api.dev.env.age                         | -   | env | dev
#   apps/api/.env | infra/env/api.dev.env + secrets/api.dev.env.age | 600 | render

# Terraform state (R2, bucket waker-backup) for infra/github: AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID / AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY of the R2 token waker-terraform-state.
-             | secrets/waker-terraform-state.env.age | -   | env
